# requestsAuth.rest:
# requests.rest
# REST Client script to test API routes.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api

# Automatically capture the token from the login response for subsequent requests
@authToken = {{loginRequest.response.body.token}}

# Capture the second user's token for use in ownership delete testing.
@otherAuthToken = {{loginSecondUser.response.body.token}}


### USER MANAGEMENT & AUTHENTICATION

## First, seed the Db

### Get all users
GET {{baseUrl}}/users


### Create a new user (with password hashing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
"username": "authenticateduser@gmail.com",
"name": "Auth User",
"password": "secret"
}

### Login as the user to obtain a JWT token
### Tag the POST request so the REST Client extension knows where to find the JWT. 
# @name loginRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "authenticateduser@gmail.com",
  "password": "secret"
}


### Test POST user email validation error (invalid email format)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
"username": "not-an-email",
"name": "Test User",
"password": "secret"
}

### Get all users
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### Get a single user by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1

### Update a user's name by username
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/authenticateduser@gmail.com
Content-Type: application/json

{
"name": "Authenticated User (Updated)"
}


### PROTECTED BLOG ROUTES (Require JWT)

### Add a new blog WITH an authentication token (Success case)
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
"author": "Authenticated Author",
"url": "https://authenticatedauthor.org/",
"title": "Secure Blog Post with Token",
"likes": 10
}

### Test POST blog failure: Try creating a blog without a token (401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/blogs
Content-Type: application/json

{
"author": "Unauthorized Author",
"url": "https://unauthoriseauthor.org/",
"title": "Should Fail",
"likes": 0
}


### OWNERSHIP TEST: 403 FORBIDDEN

### Create a SECOND user (The "Other" user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "otheruser@gmail.com",
  "name": "Other User",
  "password": "secret"
}

### Login as the SECOND user to obtain a separate token
# @name loginSecondUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "otheruser@gmail.com",
  "password": "secret"
}

### Get all blogs
GET {{baseUrl}}/blogs

### Test DELETE failure: Try to delete a blog owned by someone else (403 Forbidden)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/blogs/4
Authorization: Bearer {{otherAuthToken}}

### Test DELETE success: Delete a blog as its owner (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/blogs/4
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### PUBLIC BLOG ROUTES & ERROR HANDLING

### Get all blogs
GET {{baseUrl}}/blogs

### Update the likes of a specific blog, by id
PUT {{baseUrl}}/blogs/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
"likes": 40
}

### Test PUT error handling (Invalid likes data type)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/blogs/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
"likes": "not-a-number"
}

### Delete a blog with valid non-existing id (401 Unaurthorised) Token Missing
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/blogs/999999

### Delete a blog by malformed id (401 Unaurthorised) Token Missing
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/blogs/abc